 "notes": "95% one-sided upper limit on g_agamma from non-observation of X-rays from the magnetic white dwarf RE J0317-853 with ~40 ks of Chandra data (Dessert, Long & Safdi 2021). Curve traced from the vector paths of Fig. 1 (e-print plots/gagg_limits.pdf), the 'RE J0317-853 (this work)' observed limit for the tree-level scenario C_aee = C_agamma, i.e. the abstract's headline g_agamma < 5.5e-13 sqrt(C_agamma/C_aee) GeV^-1 for m_a < 5e-6 eV. Axis calibration verified against the quoted flat values 5.5e-13 (C_aee=C_agamma) and 4.4e-11 (W-phobic one-loop curve, not reported). Underlying constraint is on the product g_aee*g_agamma < 1.3e-25 GeV^-1; the alternative W-phobic loop-induced curve is this curve times ~79. Limit is astrophysical (axion production in the MWD core), independent of the local dark-matter density.",
